            <ArticleTitle>Relapse of B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia presenting as right aural polyp with facial and mandibular nerves palsy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>318-320</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient presenting with an ear polyp is a common finding in otorhinolaryngology practice. The common causes include chronic otitis media and cholesteatoma. We report an adult female patient with a history of acute leukaemia presenting with chronic otitis media symptoms and right ear polyp. She was subsequently diagnosed as relapse of B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia based on histopathological examination. The presentation may be similar to an inflammatory pathology of the middle ear, making it misleading.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
